"[\n  {\u0022id\u0022: \u0022C1\u0022, \u0022severity\u0022: \u0022High\u0022, \u0022issue\u0022: \u0022Ostrow\u0027s exit-interview denial of core-algorithm access vs. forensic access/transfer evidence.\u0022, \u0022claim_a\u0022: \u0022Ostrow stated at exit interview: \\\u0022I only ever touched the marketing-facing specs, I never had access to the core control algorithms - that was Priya\u0027s call to keep tight.\\\u0022\u0022, \u0022source_a\u0022: [\u0022D006\u0022, \u0022E016\u0022], \u0022claim_b\u0022: \u0022Meridian forensic report shows Ostrow\u0027s credentials accessed the Kestrel core/research repository subdirectories (containing the unfiled torque-compensation source code and tuning notebooks) on 11 occasions between March 18-April 30, 2025, and that he transferred Kestrel_Core_Algorithm_v4.2.zip and Torque_Compensation_Source.tar.gz (nearly 1.2GB combined) to a personal USB device on April 30, 2025.\u0022, \u0022source_b\u0022: [\u0022D003\u0022, \u0022E008\u0022], \u0022materiality\u0022: \u0022Directly bears on witness credibility and the knowledge/access element of the trade-secret misappropriation claim.\u0022},\n  {\u0022id\u0022: \u0022C2\u0022, \u0022severity\u0022: \u0022Medium\u0022, \u0022issue\u0022: \u0022Characterization of access as restricted/exceptional vs. standing/routine.\u0022, \u0022claim_a\u0022: \u0022Exit interview suggests Ostrow\u0027s access to core algorithms was not his to have (\\\u0022that was Priya\u0027s call to keep tight\\\u0022), implying no standing access.\u0022, \u0022source_a\u0022: [\u0022D006\u0022, \u0022E016\u0022], \u0022claim_b\u0022: \u0022Forensic report finds Ostrow\u0027s role (Senior Firmware Engineer) had standing read/write access to the core/research subdirectories and that this access \\\u0022was not exceptional or the result of a permissions error.\\\u0022\u0022, \u0022source_b\u0022: [\u0022D003\u0022], \u0022materiality\u0022: \u0022Affects whether access itself was authorized, which weakens an unauthorized-access theory even though subsequent transfer/use may still be actionable; relevant to anticipated defense argument.\u0022},\n  {\u0022id\u0022: \u0022C3\u0022, \u0022severity\u0022: \u0022High\u0022, \u0022issue\u0022: \u0022Identical unusual technical language/misspelling in Vantek\u0027s unfiled confidential draft vs. Halcyon\u0027s independently published documentation.\u0022, \u0022claim_a\u0022: \u0022Vantek\u0027s internal, unreleased Kestrel Rev. C draft (March 2025) contains an engineering note with the misspelling \\\u0022threshhold.\\\u0022\u0022, \u0022source_a\u0022: [\u0022D005\u0022], \u0022claim_b\u0022: \u0022Halcyon\u0027s publicly released Falcon-9X documentation (June 2025 beta) contains the identical misspelling \\\u0022threshhold\\\u0022 plus matching coefficients (k1=0.087, k2=0.014) and near-identical algorithm description, despite Halcyon disclosing no independent tuning methodology or dataset.\u0022, \u0022source_b\u0022: [\u0022D005\u0022], \u0022materiality\u0022: \u0022Strong circumstantial evidence undermining any independent-development defense; central to the misappropriation/copying theory and damages case.\u0022},\n  {\u0022id\u0022: \u0022C4\u0022, \u0022severity\u0022: \u0022Medium\u0022, \u0022issue\u0022: \u0022Timing/concealment of Halcyon relationship relative to resignation narrative.\u0022, \u0022claim_a\u0022: \u0022Ostrow\u0027s resignation email (May 2, 2025) frames his departure simply as accepting a new, unspecified opportunity; at exit interview (May 9, 2025) he declined to name his new employer, saying only \\\u0022a smaller company, better fit.\\\u0022\u0022, \u0022source_a\u0022: [\u0022E009\u0022, \u0022D006\u0022, \u0022E016\u0022], \u0022claim_b\u0022: \u0022Ten days before resigning, Ostrow was already on a first-name, familiar basis with Halcyon\u0027s Denise Iyer, discussing Halcyon\u0027s product line and offering to share his compensation-algorithm approach once employed there (April 22, 2025).\u0022, \u0022source_b\u0022: [\u0022E007\u0022], \u0022materiality\u0022: \u0022Suggests the Halcyon relationship and intent to use Vantek know-how predated and was concealed at the time of resignation/exit interview; relevant to premeditation and credibility.\u0022}\n]\n"